# Use Case Patterns

## Co-locate related use cases in the same file (required)

If a use case covers a sub-concern that could stand alone (e.g. hierarchy fetching broken out of center-detail fetching), define it as a separate class **in the same file** rather than a new file or a private method.

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD — FetchHierarchyUseCase lives in FetchCenterDetailUseCase.kt
class FetchCenterDetailUseCase(...) {
    private fun fetchHierarchyForCenter(...) =
        FetchHierarchyUseCase(demarcationService).execute(...)
}

class FetchHierarchyUseCase(private val demarcationService: DemarcationService) {
    fun execute(entryCode: String, depth: Int, onError: ...): List<DemarcationEntryInfo>
}

// ❌ BAD — private helper method duplicating logic that could be its own use case
class FetchCenterDetailUseCase(...) {
    private fun fetchHierarchyForCenter(...): List<DemarcationEntryInfo> { ... }
}
```

## Non-nullable service = required dependency

When a use case is dedicated to a single service, inject it as non-nullable. Reserve nullable (`Service? = null`) only for **optional features** in a parent/composite use case.

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD — FetchHierarchyUseCase always needs DemarcationService
class FetchHierarchyUseCase(private val demarcationService: DemarcationService)

// ✅ GOOD — hierarchy is optional in the composite use case
class FetchCenterDetailUseCase(
    private val centerService: CenterService,
    private val demarcationService: DemarcationService? = null,  // null = feature disabled
)
```

## Composite use cases delegate to focused use cases

A use case that coordinates multiple concerns should construct and delegate to the focused use cases rather than re-implementing their logic inline.

## Services are pure API adapters (required)

Services make HTTP calls, deserialize responses, and wrap them in `ApiResponse`. They must **not** contain view-logic such as sorting, filtering, blank-code guards, or any other business rules — those belong in the use case.

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD — service returns raw SearchingResult, no sorting
fun getEntryParents(entryCode: String, depth: Int): ApiResponse<SearchingResult<DemarcationEntryInfo>> {
    // HTTP call + deserialize + wrap in ApiResponse
}

// ✅ GOOD — use case owns sort and blank guard
fun execute(entryCode: String, ...): List<DemarcationEntryInfo> {
    if (entryCode.isBlank()) return emptyList()
    val response = demarcationService.getEntryParents(entryCode, depth)
    return response.payload?.content?.records.orEmpty()
        .sortedBy { it.demarcationLevel?.code ?: Int.MAX_VALUE }
}

// ❌ BAD — service sorts results before returning
fun getEntryParents(...): ApiResponse<List<DemarcationEntryInfo>> {
    val entries = page.records.orEmpty().sortedBy { it.demarcationLevel?.code ?: Int.MAX_VALUE }
    return hierarchyResponse(entries)
}
```
